01:40.600 --> 01:43.580
The Japanese Junior Youth team won the world title four years ago.

01:44.060 --> 01:49.580
These players of soccer's golden age have begun to play professionally.

01:50.210 --> 01:53.890
Ohzora Tsubasa changed his stage from Brazil to Spain.

01:54.880 --> 01:59.420
Hyuga Kojiro transferred to the Italian League powerhouse, Piemonte.

01:59.420 --> 02:01.860
The first to move overseas

02:01.860 --> 02:07.410
and now the starting goalie for the German FC Grünwald, Wakabayashi Genzo.

02:08.400 --> 02:12.420
Misaki Taro, the J-League rookie and last year's MVP,

02:12.420 --> 02:14.800
has already agreed to challenge for the French League.

02:14.800 --> 02:17.420
He is getting offers from multiple teams.

02:18.470 --> 02:23.420
Other players are now following in their footsteps by playing in the J-League.

02:23.420 --> 02:28.410
The time has finally come for them to aim for the top of the world.

02:29.710 --> 02:36.170
To prove their ability to the world... We must win against the Dutch first.

02:40.460 --> 02:45.620
<b>The Golden Age of Hope</b>

02:40.460 --> 02:45.620
<b>The Golden Age of Hope</b>

02:45.620 --> 02:48.300
 -Germany- FC Grünwald Practice Field

02:49.140 --> 02:55.390
Gen-san, I hear Japan is having a training match with the Dutch before the International Cup.

02:55.390 --> 02:56.020
Yeah.

02:56.020 --> 03:00.810
The Netherlands is among the top teams in Europe.

03:00.810 --> 03:04.350
They weren't lucky and got eliminated in International Cup prelims,

03:04.350 --> 03:08.020
but their skills are top class, without a doubt.

03:08.020 --> 03:12.580
They didn't have to pick such a tough opponent for a training match!

03:14.040 --> 03:15.300
Right.

03:16.510 --> 03:17.950
What's so funny?

03:17.950 --> 03:22.490
There's a guy I know in the Japanese Football Association who'd come up with such an idea.

03:24.610 --> 03:27.370
That guy must be a huge idiot!

03:27.370 --> 03:28.020
Yeah.

03:29.220 --> 03:31.500
Maybe he is.

03:32.180 --> 03:34.660
 -France- Paris

03:35.420 --> 03:38.060
Picking the Netherlands for a training match...

03:40.560 --> 03:42.410
That's exactly what I'd expect from Katagiri-san.

03:42.940 --> 03:45.900
 -Italy- FC Piemonte Practice Field

03:45.900 --> 03:49.010
Willem must be among the members of the Netherlands team.

03:53.510 --> 03:54.300
All right!

03:54.300 --> 03:58.050
I'll definitely get a starting position on the Japanese team!

03:58.740 --> 04:02.700
 Spain- FC Cataluña Practice Field

03:59.780 --> 04:02.940
Bernhardt-san and Albert-san are representing the Netherlands.

04:03.560 --> 04:07.420
The Dutch team has other internationally renowned players as well.

04:08.290 --> 04:09.740
I want to challenge them.

04:09.740 --> 04:11.460
I want to challenge the Dutch team, too!

04:14.020 --> 04:15.060
Tsubasa!

04:15.060 --> 04:16.490
Yes?

04:16.490 --> 04:19.540
Someone from the Japanese Football Association called.

04:19.540 --> 04:20.440
What?

04:22.820 --> 04:25.100
Japanese Football Association

04:22.820 --> 04:25.100
Fairy Tale Corporation

04:22.820 --> 04:25.100
Emishi Film Corporation

04:25.580 --> 04:26.780
Katagiri-kun.

04:26.790 --> 04:33.100
As you requested, we sent invitations to Ohzora, Wakabayashi, Hyuga, and Misaki.

04:33.730 --> 04:35.220
Thank you.

04:35.220 --> 04:40.270
The document in front of you is the list of other candidates.

04:41.030 --> 04:42.980
What is the meaning of this?

04:42.980 --> 04:47.980
These are the strongest candidates for the Japanese team.

04:47.980 --> 04:49.500
Any problem?

04:50.520 --> 04:52.770
Of course there is!

04:52.770 --> 04:56.420
This is exactly the same lineup from the Junior Youth team four years ago.

04:56.420 --> 04:58.980
Ohzora and others were approved

04:58.980 --> 05:02.420
because they've proven themselves internationally, despite their age.

05:02.420 --> 05:06.620
But the remaining members are all rookies in the J-League!

05:06.620 --> 05:11.080
What are you thinking by nominating these unproven players?

05:11.080 --> 05:13.010
It is true they are unproven.

05:13.010 --> 05:18.460
However, they have amazing potential, just like our players who went overseas.

05:18.930 --> 05:21.030
I don't care about their potentials.

05:21.030 --> 05:24.150
We only care about their current abilities.

05:24.150 --> 05:26.730
Even if they have promising futures,

05:26.730 --> 05:29.930
the association's decision-making ability will be questioned

05:29.930 --> 05:32.210
if we put them up against the Netherlands!

05:32.940 --> 05:34.960
I agree, Chairman!

05:34.960 --> 05:37.490
Please convince him.

05:39.010 --> 05:40.840
What do you say, Katagiri-kun?

05:40.840 --> 05:44.220
Would you reconsider?

05:44.220 --> 05:45.670
No.

05:45.670 --> 05:48.220
These are the best members I have chosen.

05:48.950 --> 05:54.360
We must think about the future of Japanese soccer.

05:54.360 --> 05:57.460
That is our duty.

06:00.030 --> 06:01.170
Am I wrong?

06:01.170 --> 06:03.460
You have a point.

06:03.460 --> 06:07.780
But it doesn't have to be on a critical time line like now, before the International Cup.

06:07.780 --> 06:11.580
Isn't it necessary <i>because</i> the timing is critical?

06:11.580 --> 06:14.580
I support Katagiri's decision.

06:16.180 --> 06:17.380
Coach Louvois...

06:18.310 --> 06:21.720
The winning team for the Junior Youth World Tournament, huh?

06:23.400 --> 06:25.390
Interesting.

06:25.390 --> 06:28.420
I want to test promising youth while they're young.

06:28.420 --> 06:33.950
As the coach of the Japanese team, I will decide upon the representatives

06:33.950 --> 06:37.420
after seeing as many players as I can before the International Cup.

06:37.420 --> 06:39.940
Age is not important!

06:39.940 --> 06:41.820
B-But...

06:41.820 --> 06:44.410
No objections, Chairman?

06:44.780 --> 06:45.420
None.

06:45.850 --> 06:46.820
Very well.

06:53.390 --> 06:54.220
Coach.

06:56.890 --> 06:58.330
Thank you.

06:58.330 --> 07:00.310
You don't have to thank me.

07:00.740 --> 07:05.110
It was my honest opinion as the coach.

07:06.460 --> 07:10.410
You said they are the best members to represent Japan.

07:10.410 --> 07:12.020
I'm looking forward to them.

07:13.340 --> 07:14.130
Okay.

07:17.250 --> 07:19.770
Man, it brings back memories.

07:19.770 --> 07:23.570
Remember how we fought over the field when we were in elementary school?

07:24.650 --> 07:25.860
Yeah.

07:25.860 --> 07:28.280
That was when Tsubasa transferred here.

07:28.280 --> 07:30.940
Tsubasa sure was good in that game.

07:31.270 --> 07:32.860
We were shocked!

07:33.750 --> 07:35.900
Tsubasa is coming back, right?

07:35.900 --> 07:37.100
Yeah.

07:37.100 --> 07:38.130
Today.

07:42.130 --> 07:44.900
It's been so long since I last saw him.

07:44.900 --> 07:47.140
<b>{TS0747}Ohzora</b>

07:47.140 --> 07:50.910
You're such a big help, Sanae-chan.

07:50.910 --> 07:53.240
Oh, it's nothing.

07:53.580 --> 07:55.940
Okay, it's done!

08:03.380 --> 08:05.230
Um, Auntie.

08:05.230 --> 08:07.870
I'll go wait outside.

08:09.840 --> 08:15.540
Ah, she must be really longing to see him again after all this time.

08:26.250 --> 08:27.560
Tsubasa-kun...

08:30.020 --> 08:31.300
Sanae-chan!

08:33.820 --> 08:35.240
Welcome back.

08:35.890 --> 08:37.090
It's good to be back.

08:37.090 --> 08:38.760
It's been four years.

08:38.760 --> 08:39.780
Yeah.

08:40.260 --> 08:41.780
You've grown.

08:42.500 --> 08:43.620
Really?

08:43.910 --> 08:45.620
Yes, you have.

08:45.620 --> 08:48.990
And you don't look as bossy as I remembered.

08:49.460 --> 08:50.950
Hey!

08:59.740 --> 09:01.460
What's up, Ishizaki?

09:01.460 --> 09:03.360
To your right!

09:04.420 --> 09:06.460
Whoa, whoa!

09:08.100 --> 09:10.740
Ishizaki, you haven't improved at all!

09:11.180 --> 09:12.260
Shut up!

09:14.870 --> 09:18.260
It's been years since we all gathered like this.

09:18.260 --> 09:19.310
Yeah.

09:19.310 --> 09:22.040
You're all J-Leaguers now, after all.

09:22.040 --> 09:25.470
Tsubasa, Hyuga, and Wakabayashi-san are superstars now.

09:25.470 --> 09:28.260
Is that superstar really coming here?

09:28.260 --> 09:30.020
You can all count on me!

09:30.020 --> 09:35.420
I told my manager to bring him back without telling him we're here.

09:36.370 --> 09:38.280
Tsubasa is going to be surprised!

09:38.280 --> 09:40.340
I can't wait to see him!

09:40.340 --> 09:42.330
Oh! Here they come!

09:45.460 --> 09:46.940
You guys!

09:46.940 --> 09:49.310
Tsubasa! We've been waiting for you!

09:50.480 --> 09:52.260
You all came back.

09:52.260 --> 09:53.950
Of course!

09:53.950 --> 09:59.140
You're coming back, so this has to be the place to wait for you!

09:59.140 --> 10:00.750
Right.

10:00.750 --> 10:04.150
This is where our soccer careers began.

10:04.150 --> 10:05.670
As I thought, you'd all be here.

10:06.860 --> 10:09.290
Wakabayashi-kun!

10:10.770 --> 10:12.780
Wakabayashi-kun, you're back, too?

10:12.780 --> 10:15.060
It's been so long, Tsubasa.

10:15.060 --> 10:15.890
Yeah.

10:15.890 --> 10:19.860
If you're also back to Japan, does that mean...

10:19.860 --> 10:20.980
Yeah.

10:20.980 --> 10:23.380
I was invited to represent Japan.

10:23.380 --> 10:24.910
Ah!

10:24.910 --> 10:28.210
You guys are both candidates for the Japanese team?

10:28.210 --> 10:31.390
Hyuga and Misaki must have been invited too.

10:31.390 --> 10:34.260
You guys are way out of my league.

10:34.260 --> 10:36.150
That's not true!

10:36.150 --> 10:37.900
You don't have to comfort me.

10:38.400 --> 10:40.200
Just watch!

10:40.200 --> 10:44.440
I'll represent Japan one day and become a star!

10:44.440 --> 10:49.900
The national team aside, you still haven't played a single official game in J-League!

10:49.900 --> 10:53.360
Shut up! Don't mention that!

10:53.360 --> 10:56.580
I mean, Urabe is in the same situation.

10:56.580 --> 10:58.660
You're one to talk!

10:59.090 --> 11:00.960
You're nothing but talk...

11:00.960 --> 11:02.660
This sure brings back memories.

11:02.660 --> 11:07.390
It feels like I just played soccer with them yesterday.

11:14.800 --> 11:16.220
What is it, Tsubasa?

11:16.660 --> 11:19.420
All right! Let's play soccer, guys!

11:20.470 --> 11:22.180
We're all gathered here in one place.

11:22.180 --> 11:24.200
{shabetteru}It'd be a waste if we're just here to talk.

11:24.200 --> 11:26.870
That's right. Let's play a mock game.

11:26.870 --> 11:29.700
Show us how much you've improved.

11:29.700 --> 11:30.920
Fine!

11:30.920 --> 11:34.880
You'd better be ready for my magnificent technique!

11:37.050 --> 11:39.420
Tsubasa! Pass me the ball!

11:39.420 --> 11:40.250
Sure!

11:45.820 --> 11:47.340
Kisugi, run forward!

11:47.340 --> 11:49.900
Ishizaki! Contain him!

11:52.620 --> 11:55.840
From Brazil to Spain, and now, the Japanese team.

11:55.840 --> 11:58.370
He keeps rising to a higher stage,

11:58.370 --> 12:00.630
but he's still the old Tsubasa-kun we all know.

12:00.630 --> 12:03.100
No, it's not just Tsubasa-kun.

12:03.100 --> 12:05.580
None of them changed.

12:05.580 --> 12:07.090
Ishizaki!

12:07.090 --> 12:08.060
All right!

12:08.400 --> 12:10.500
You messed up, Ishizaki.

12:10.500 --> 12:12.100
I know, damn it!

12:15.410 --> 12:16.780
It's Katagiri-san.

12:20.370 --> 12:24.420
There's something I want to let you know as soon as possible.

12:24.910 --> 12:28.250
If you came all the way here, that means...

12:28.250 --> 12:29.850
it's about the Dutch game, isn't it?

12:29.850 --> 12:30.660
Yes.

12:30.660 --> 12:33.380
I want to challenge the Dutch team, too!

12:33.380 --> 12:37.900
I'm here to tell you my plan against the Dutch team.

12:37.900 --> 12:40.260
Your plan?

12:40.260 --> 12:47.740
I want you guys, the Junior Youth World Champions, to face the Dutch team.

12:47.740 --> 12:49.120
What?

12:49.120 --> 12:54.260
Izawa, Taki, Kisugi, Morisaki, Takasugi, and Ishizaki.

12:54.260 --> 12:57.210
You should get official invitations soon.

12:57.210 --> 12:59.020
Be prepared.

13:04.980 --> 13:06.940
I'm going to represent Japan?

13:07.530 --> 13:08.780
Is he serious?

13:09.420 --> 13:11.850
What's wrong? Are you scared?

13:11.850 --> 13:16.480
Didn't you just say you were going to be a star on the Japanese team?

13:18.450 --> 13:19.820
Yeah!

13:19.820 --> 13:23.410
Our dream is winning the International Cup!

13:23.410 --> 13:24.470
It's a chance for me.

13:24.470 --> 13:26.020
I'm not scared!

13:26.480 --> 13:27.920
That's the spirit.

13:27.920 --> 13:28.970
All right!

13:28.970 --> 13:31.020
Let's beat the Netherlands together!

13:31.020 --> 13:32.420
Yeah!

13:35.110 --> 13:39.060
The team for the training game against the Netherlands is made up entirely of rookies.

13:39.060 --> 13:43.220
Do you really stand a chance against the powerhouse that the Dutch team is?

13:44.430 --> 13:48.540
Or does the association have something up their sleeves?

13:49.550 --> 13:52.840
I am willing to offer you a personal opinion.

13:52.840 --> 13:53.860
Please.

13:53.860 --> 13:58.380
It's because I see the potential for them to become International Cup champions.

14:05.820 --> 14:09.140
 Fukushima Prefecture, J-Village

14:09.670 --> 14:14.660
As you all know, we, as the host of the next International Cup,

14:14.660 --> 14:19.310
will skip the preliminaries and start playing directly in the tournament.

14:19.310 --> 14:22.170
In other words, we will be playing against powerhouse teams

14:22.170 --> 14:24.700
who have already won their qualifying matches.

14:24.700 --> 14:29.700
The Japanese team requires the power to play evenly against such teams.

14:29.700 --> 14:33.080
The Dutch team, also known as the Uncrowned Powerhouse,

14:33.080 --> 14:35.900
{kimi tachi}is the best opponent to gauge your abilities.

14:36.710 --> 14:39.010
If you can't stand up to them,

14:39.010 --> 14:42.820
you won't possibly perform well in the International Cup.

14:42.820 --> 14:44.100
You must beat them!

14:44.100 --> 14:45.820
Think only about winning!

14:46.310 --> 14:50.500
This is your most important task against the Dutch..

14:52.680 --> 14:55.350
We've received a dispute from the Dutch team.

14:55.350 --> 15:01.340
They said they won't bring their regular members to play against our lineup.

15:03.020 --> 15:05.020
What are you going to do about it?

15:05.020 --> 15:06.660
I'll go to the Netherlands.

15:10.780 --> 15:12.020
This is the time.

15:13.140 --> 15:15.780
This is the time to change Japanese soccer.

15:16.140 --> 15:20.020
Japan

15:16.140 --> 15:20.020
South Korea

15:24.420 --> 15:24.980
Damn!

15:24.980 --> 15:27.110
Here's the Japanese ace striker, Katagiri.

15:27.110 --> 15:29.530
He's covered by three defenders and can't receive any passes!

15:30.720 --> 15:32.880
Oh, Takayama has run into an open space!

15:32.880 --> 15:33.100
He shoots!

15:34.150 --> 15:36.660
But the shooting course was too easy to read!

15:36.660 --> 15:38.200
Is it hopeless?

15:38.200 --> 15:41.700
Is Japan powerless with Katagiri contained?

15:42.420 --> 15:43.900
There's not much of the injury time left!

15:45.100 --> 15:47.380
Katagiri slides and shoots!

15:47.860 --> 15:49.350
It bounced off the bar!

15:49.350 --> 15:50.710
No goal!

15:53.230 --> 15:55.280
Ah, the game is over.

15:55.280 --> 15:56.460
Total defeat for Japan.

15:56.460 --> 15:58.930
3-0 against their rival, South Korea.

15:58.930 --> 16:01.980
Japan fails to overcome the Asian obstacle again.

16:01.980 --> 16:06.150
Japan has failed to advance past the International Cup Asia Preliminaries once again!

16:09.810 --> 16:12.370
Individual skill alone was not enough.

16:12.830 --> 16:15.070
I got taught a lesson back then.

16:16.140 --> 16:20.140
<b>Elementary Football Tournament</b>

16:16.460 --> 16:19.690
After retirement, I joined the Japanese Football Association,

16:19.690 --> 16:23.670
and continued to think about how to make Japan stronger.

16:23.670 --> 16:26.510
So, I scouted the next generation of players.

16:28.820 --> 16:30.780
Then, I met them.

16:31.400 --> 16:34.380
Hyuga, Wakabayashi, and Misaki.

16:35.410 --> 16:38.900
It was a generation filled with talent,

16:38.900 --> 16:42.670
but it was Ohzora Tsubasa who shined the most.

16:43.640 --> 16:47.490
And when they became Junior Youth World Champions,

16:47.490 --> 16:53.980
I determined that they would become the generation that will truly change Japanese soccer.

16:54.430 --> 16:57.880
I will have them aim for the top of the world.

16:57.880 --> 17:02.100
For that purpose, they must get used to playing against tough opponents.

17:07.430 --> 17:08.850
Did you hear?

17:08.850 --> 17:12.680
The Dutch team might not bring their regular members.

17:13.040 --> 17:13.820
Yeah.

17:13.820 --> 17:16.730
I hear Katagiri-san flew to the Netherlands,

17:16.730 --> 17:19.460
but we still don't know what will happen.

17:19.460 --> 17:21.520
They're looking down on us!

17:21.520 --> 17:24.490
Are they saying we don't stand a chance?

17:24.490 --> 17:26.850
We can't blame them for thinking that way.

17:26.850 --> 17:28.140
Misugi!

17:28.610 --> 17:31.590
We're still lacking in experience and accomplishment.

17:31.590 --> 17:34.300
There's nothing strange about the Dutch not taking us seriously.

17:39.450 --> 17:41.500
Why are you all whining?

17:41.500 --> 17:43.420
Who cares about our opponents?

17:43.420 --> 17:46.260
We'll just crush whoever shows up!

17:46.260 --> 17:48.070
If a bunch of second-rate players show up,

17:48.070 --> 17:50.940
we'll just beat them and drag their top team here!

17:51.390 --> 17:52.340
He's right.

17:52.340 --> 17:56.420
No matter who we're up against, we'll play our own soccer.

17:56.420 --> 17:59.140
Let's just get prepared for that!

17:59.140 --> 18:00.460
Tsubasa...

18:00.460 --> 18:03.460
We just have to give it our all with what we've got.

18:03.460 --> 18:04.440
Come on.

18:04.440 --> 18:05.460
Let's start the practice!

18:05.940 --> 18:07.300
Yeah!

18:08.610 --> 18:10.750
"Our own soccer," huh?

18:11.650 --> 18:15.830
There is something remarkable about the growth of Japanese soccer in recent years.

18:15.830 --> 18:20.240
{tsui ni}You have even landed the rights to host the International Cup.

18:20.240 --> 18:27.740
We were trying to gather the best Dutch players for this training game out of respect.

18:27.740 --> 18:31.900
But this is how you return the favor?

18:31.900 --> 18:33.500
It's insulting!

18:33.500 --> 18:38.860
They are just as talented as any of our past representatives.

18:39.390 --> 18:42.270
We are not taking the Dutch team lightly.

18:42.790 --> 18:46.010
We can't send our regular members! No matter what you say!

18:46.010 --> 18:47.100
Chairman!

18:47.520 --> 18:49.780
There's nothing more to talk about.

18:49.780 --> 18:51.100
Get out!

18:54.860 --> 18:56.090
That's no good!

18:56.090 --> 18:58.020
Move up faster!

18:58.020 --> 18:59.870
The Dutch are fast!

18:59.870 --> 19:02.040
All you have to do is advance together!

19:08.700 --> 19:10.430
Still too slow!

19:10.430 --> 19:12.420
Run full speed to the center of the field!

19:16.740 --> 19:17.960
Okay!

19:17.960 --> 19:18.940
Take a break!

19:21.020 --> 19:23.240
So you came.

19:23.240 --> 19:27.260
Katagiri asked me to take a look at them.

19:32.180 --> 19:34.710
So, what do you think?

19:35.130 --> 19:36.380
Let's see...

19:36.840 --> 19:39.280
Well, probably the same as you.

19:40.060 --> 19:42.110
You're going back already?

19:42.110 --> 19:45.540
Yeah, you wouldn't want me to see too much, right?

19:45.540 --> 19:48.810
I'm a coach from the opposing team, after all.

19:48.810 --> 19:50.660
I just came by for a greeting.

19:50.660 --> 19:51.580
See you later.

19:54.840 --> 19:57.490
It's a waste of time to continue this meeting.

19:58.220 --> 20:00.330
I'm taking my leave.

20:07.820 --> 20:11.140
Chairman, you have a phone call from Coach Bernevelt.

20:12.140 --> 20:14.040
From the coach?

20:14.040 --> 20:15.330
Put him through.

20:16.450 --> 20:18.160
What is it, Coach?

20:18.160 --> 20:19.750
Calling me in person...

20:19.750 --> 20:22.980
Chairman, about the training match again Japan...

20:23.480 --> 20:27.110
I've decided to go with the regular members as we originally planned.

20:27.110 --> 20:28.100
What?

20:28.100 --> 20:31.980
I believe the right to select the players was given to me.

20:31.980 --> 20:33.650
Yes, but...

20:33.650 --> 20:35.880
Is Katagiri with you right now?

20:35.880 --> 20:37.240
I want to talk to him.

20:38.690 --> 20:40.100
Please wait.

20:41.240 --> 20:42.500
I'm Katagiri.

20:42.500 --> 20:47.940
You said Japan will become a rival to the Netherlands in the near future, didn't you?

20:47.940 --> 20:48.610
Yes.

20:49.330 --> 20:54.500
I went to check out the Japanese team in order to confirm your claims.

20:54.540 --> 20:56.090
Coach...

20:56.090 --> 20:58.070
You're in Japan right now?

20:58.070 --> 20:59.270
Yes.

20:59.270 --> 21:01.210
It's a great team.

21:01.210 --> 21:02.850
Thank you.

21:02.850 --> 21:05.260
Mr. Katagiri, I promise you...

21:05.940 --> 21:11.260
I will bring the best players from the Netherlands with me to Japan.

21:11.770 --> 21:12.990
Is that so?

21:12.990 --> 21:13.780
Yes.

21:14.320 --> 21:16.140
But I have to warn you.

21:16.140 --> 21:19.750
I don't intend to go easy on you, so be prepared.

21:21.460 --> 21:23.300
I'll look forward to it.

21:23.300 --> 21:25.680
Well then, good bye.

21:28.290 --> 21:30.120
This is going to get interesting.

21:50.420 --> 21:52.140
Come, the Netherlands!

21:53.140 --> 21:55.140
We'll show you the way we play soccer!

21:55.580 --> 21:58.920
And we'll win that way!

22:04.020 --> 22:11.540
Preview

22:05.100 --> 22:08.620
The training camp began with the Dutch game in sight.

22:09.480 --> 22:13.110
For that reason, Katagiri-san brought a player from Italy with him.

22:13.110 --> 22:15.700
He's Aoi Shingo from FC Lombardy.

22:15.720 --> 22:19.980
We were encouraged by Shingo, who optimistically faced tough training.

22:19.980 --> 22:21.460
Let's fight together!

22:21.460 --> 22:24.290
Let's beat the Dutch and aim for the top!

22:25.020 --> 22:26.860
Next time, on Captain Tsubasa:

22:25.980 --> 22:34.100
Aoi Shingo Takes the Stage!

22:26.860 --> 22:28.460
Aoi Shingo Takes the Stage!

22:28.460 --> 22:29.310
